description:
This PR changes the `EventStream.addEventMonitorCallback()` method from not returning anything to returning the callback passed to it.

This is a slight improvement for development that makes it easier to use `addEventMonitorCallback` and `delEventFilterCallback` together with arrow functions like so:

```
const cb = eventStream.addEventMonitorCallback('target', () => {
 // this is a callback
});
eventStream.delEventFilterCallback(cb);
```

## Intent
Small improvement to the `EventStream` to make it easier to use in #233 and further work.

This is a follow-up to #105 that incorporates the type changes seen in #89.

## Intent
- Part of #83 

## Approach
- This takes the type `file` struct in `internal/services/api/files.go` and incorporates it into the frontend types

## Directions for Reviewers
- Check the added types and see if they match the Go struct in `internal/services/api/files.go`

If you'd like to verify the usage you can add the following to a frontend Vue component:

```
import { useApi } from 'src/api/client';

const api = useApi();

const files = async() => {
  const response = await api.files.get({ pathname: 'web/src/api' });
  console.log(response);
};

files();
```

This PR adds the Files API resource to the frontend `PublishingClientApi` and the associated type definitions.

## Intent
- Resolves #83 

## Approach
- The Files resource uses the same pattern started in the `Accounts.ts` resource
- `get()` was used over `getAll()` since the `/api/files` endpoint returns a single File and not an array of files
- A new pattern is established here for `URLSearchParams`
  - Axios supports using an Object for params rather than creating a string: ["Must be a plain object or a URLSearchParams object NOTE: params that are null or undefined are not rendered in the URL."](https://axios-http.com/docs/req_config)
- Inline typing is used for the Resource methods since they are only defined and used in one spot (the parameters and return structure - see `web/src/api/resources/Accounts.ts`) and it isn't necessary to add to the types files.

## Directions for Reviewers
- Check the added types and see if they match the Go struct in `internal/services/api/files.go`
- Consider the new pattern introduced for handling and typing `URLSearchParams`

If you'd like to verify the usage you can add the following to a frontend Vue component:

```
import { useApi } from 'src/api/client';

const api = useApi();

const files = async() => {
  const response = await api.files.get({ pathname: 'web/src/api' });
  console.log(response);
};

files();
```
